{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06PT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y} \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{Y} \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-locally-quasi-finite-permanence}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:48f516cf28842e722de23b8904e3fb3f52dcc44f785daed5bbb433af2fb34461", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4acaf4126b3d76db0ac952c4cf1651927c5392bc75ee161f81789e18491e1fee", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be morphisms\nof algebraic stacks. Assume that <MATH_0002>\nis locally quasi-finite and <MATH_0003> is quasi-DM.\nThen <MATH_0004> is locally quasi-finite.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:cf07a3cb323b718ebefbebd57939a00bb2bfcfda678119323c6faca6dac0c23e", "unit_id": "tag:06UG:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06PT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$$\n\\mathcal{X} \\longrightarrow\n\\mathcal{X} \\times_\\mathcal{Z} \\mathcal{Y} \\longrightarrow\n\\mathcal{Y}\n$$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{Y} \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-base-change-locally-quasi-finite}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-semi-diagonal}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-composition-locally-quasi-finite}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:85d61ad7600fd6ccfa3fbab6a8976ae74ec70b157858e8be127b327b13bf846a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b0b8f688e29fcdf0159f8d31ff9748e52adbb83c24dcb5b1e22a61aba1bbc529", "source_text": "Write <MATH_0001> as the composition\n<MATH_0002>\nThe second arrow is locally quasi-finite as a base change of\n<MATH_0003>, see\nLemma <REF_0001>.\nThe first arrow is locally quasi-finite by\nLemma <REF_0002>\nas <MATH_0004> is quasi-DM.\nHence <MATH_0005> is locally quasi-finite by\nLemma <REF_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:cf664cf281957770ca7d0ff5733e05e2d452811636770dfdb0ac96bead1e2c31", "unit_id": "tag:06UG:proof"}
